# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SiteOps dashboard environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Everything in this file is browser-visible:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the JavaScript bundle at build time and
# served to every visitor. A secret placed here is a published secret.
#
# Server configuration — the database URI, the auth secret, the mail API key —
# belongs to siteOps-server and is never read by this project. See that repo's
# `.env.example`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Origin of the SiteOps API this dashboard talks to.
#
# The browser never calls it directly. `next.config.ts` rewrites `/api/*` onto
# this origin, so every request the browser makes is same-origin and the session
# cookie is set by — and sent back to — this app's own host. That is not a
# performance choice: the cookie is HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax, and a browser
# refuses to store a Lax cookie that arrives on a cross-site response. Pointing
# the browser straight at another registrable domain (a Vercel app calling a
# Render API, say) makes sign-in return 200 and then silently drop the session.
#
# Server components still call this origin directly, forwarding the browser's
# Cookie header themselves. See `src/lib/api-base.ts`.
#
# In production: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://siteops-server.onrender.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Public origin of this app. Used to build absolute links back to itself.
#
# In production: NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://siteops-client.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
